/target
# Filled-in secrets. README walks users through `cp .env.example .env` and then
# writing JWT_SECRET and MASTER_KEY into it, so a stray `git add -A` would have
# committed the signing key and the at-rest encryption key. `.env.*` also covers
# .env.local / .env.production; the negation keeps the tracked template, which
# docker-compose and the README both reference by name.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
# Private key material. Every documented cert path (cert-init --output-dir,
# the cluster TOMLs, the e2e scripts' mktemp dirs) lands outside the worktree,
# but `cert-init` takes an arbitrary output dir and TLS config is hand-edited,
# so a relative path is one typo away. No tracked file matches either glob.
*.pem
*.key
*.swp
*.swo
.DS_Store
node_modules/
web/admin-ui/dist/
# Keep the directory itself tracked: crates/waf-api embeds it via rust-embed,
# whose derive macro fails to compile when the folder is absent. Without this,
# a fresh checkout cannot build waf-api at all.
!web/admin-ui/dist/.gitkeep
# ip2region xdb binary data files — download with `prx-waf geoip download`
data/*.xdb

# Python cache
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo

# Root-level tools/ was a duplicate of rules/tools/ — canonical path is rules/tools/
/tools/
.claude/worktrees/
